course: dictionary
lesson: 4919
title: Immigration and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Immigration is a word with three meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one. Read the clues first. «Immigration means people moving to live in another country; countries have rules about it, and people disagree about those rules.» Here the clues are moving, live and another country, so it means coming to live in a new country.
explain: The word can also mean the place at an airport or border where officers check passports. Travellers «go through immigration» before they can enter. If the sentence talks about queues, passports or officers, the word means that place.
explain: The word can mean the rules too, and the government department that makes and checks them. «Immigration rules» are the laws about who may live in a country. Ask yourself: is this about a person moving, a place, or rules? The answer tells you the meaning.
fact: Immigration means coming to live in a new country from another country.
fact: At an airport or border, «immigration» is the place where officials check passports and visas.
fact: An «immigration officer» is the person who checks people's papers when they arrive.
fact: Immigration rules are set by a country's government, and people do not always agree about them.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Immigration means people moving to live in another country.» What does immigration mean here? | Packing a suitcase for a trip | *Coming to live in a new country from another country | A kind of passport | Going on a short holiday abroad
exercise: Sam waits to «go through immigration» at the airport. Where is Sam? | *At the place where officials check passports | In a shop choosing sweets | At a train station buying a ticket | On a bus going into town
exercise: «Countries have rules about it, and people disagree about those rules.» Find and copy one word that shows people do not all agree. | countries | rules | moving | *disagree
test: What is the job of an immigration officer? | Sells tickets on a bus | *Checks passports and visas when people arrive in a country | Teaches maths at a school | Cooks food at an airport
test: What are «immigration rules»? | Recipes for cakes and biscuits | *Laws and government rules about who may come to live in a country | Maps of the world's oceans | Timetables for trains and planes
exam: Which sentence uses immigration to mean the rules? | Ella moved from Spain to live in Leeds with her family | Sam queued at immigration for an hour | *The government changed the immigration rules this year
